\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 I've written the three files and saved them rather than pasting them here, since they're long. The home page case studies, the menu and the opening got the most detail.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Case studies on the home page:
\f0\b0  there are three layouts. The text sits on rows at fixed fractions of the screen height (one sixth, half, two thirds, five sixths), each pushed down by one gutter. The thumbnail is a small window onto the full image. Clicking a project grows that window to full screen over 1.5s, and the same image becomes the case study's hero.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Menu:
\f0\b0  four white panels close in to leave a centered portrait window, 30% of the screen wide with 80px above and below. The page shrinks into it (to 0.905 on a 900px-tall screen). Pointing at a link previews that page inside the window.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Loader:
\f0\b0  the full one runs on a first visit, or when the last visit was over 24 hours ago, and takes about 4.8s. It waits for 10 full-width case study images and the hero video. It's flagged "do not copy", with a note on loading those behind a readable first screen instead.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Banned patterns found:
\f0\b0  a custom cursor, frosted buttons and header, a blurred glow in the hero, and a rotating clock in the header. The work page also shows a client logo on each row; it isn't a logo wall, but I flagged it so it doesn't become one.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 How values were read:
\f0\b0  the browser tab was only 752px wide, so I loaded the site inside a frame set to 1440 and 390 wide to take measurements. 1024 values are worked out from the CSS rules. The tab then went to the background, which stops animations from playing. From that point, motion timings come straight from the site's animation code, which gives exact durations and eases, and everything is tagged.\
